  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In presence of sunlight CFC&rsquo;s molecule divides &amp; release chlorine free radical, which react with ozone give chlorine monoxide radical (ClO) and oxygen</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>UV</mi></mover><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#729;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#729;</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mi>ClO</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>ClO</mi><mo>&#8729;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
